     1,
     "Dear all,\r<br>\r<br>I am attempting to add vertical lines between the point with Y\r<br>(defined by a variable) and X (defined by another variable in the same\r<br>row with the Y variable) and the other point (with Y = 0 and X with\r<br>same value of the first point).\r<br>\r<br>I tried geom_segments(), but I failed to reach my object. I expected\r<br>to hearing from your advice/directions.\r<br>\r<br>Thanks a lot.\r<br>\r<br>################################################################################\r<br># codes I tried\r<br># (1) this can generate the point plot, correctly. But, I would like\r<br>to have lines link the points to X axes.\r<br>pi.plot &lt;- qplot(position, fst , data = final.res, geom = &quot;point&quot;,\r<br>group = chrom,\r<br>                 colour = col, xlab = &quot;chromosome&quot;, ylab = &quot;SNP\r<br>density (snps/10k)&quot;) + facet_grid(chrom ~., scales = &quot;free_x&quot;)\r<br>(pi.plot)\r<br>\r<br>\r<br># (2) this code failed\r<br>pi.plot &lt;- qplot(position, fst , data = final.res, geom = &quot;point&quot;,\r<br>group = chrom,\r<br>                 colour = col, xlab = &quot;chromosome&quot;, ylab = &quot;SNP\r<br>density (snps/10k)&quot;) + segments(aes(x0 = position, y0 = 0, x1 =\r<br>position, y1 = fst)) + facet_grid(chrom ~., scales = &quot;free_x&quot;)\r<br>(pi.plot)\r<br>\r<br># or\r<br>\r<br>pi.plot + geom_segment(aes(xend = position, yend = fst),\r<br>arrow=arrow(length=unit(0.1,&quot;cm&quot;)))\r<br>\r<br>###############################################################################\r<br># my data set\r<br>\r<br>row.names\tchrom\tposition\tprob\tlog10.PO.\talpha\tfst\tcol\r<br>1\t62\t1\t1244475\t0.97099\t1.52470\t1.7144\t0.78278\tTRUE\r<br>2\t97\t1\t1945950\t0.95299\t1.30690\t1.6313\t0.76964\tTRUE\r<br>3\t128\t1\t2572416\t0.98120\t1.71750\t1.7728\t0.79094\tTRUE\r<br>4\t137\t1\t2753011\t0.97239\t1.54680\t1.7115\t0.78234\tTRUE\r<br>5\t379\t1\t7639640\t0.97620\t1.61290\t1.7330\t0.78564\tTRUE\r<br>6\t416\t1\t83